+# Export saved sessions
+
+Export a saved Gemini conversation in an open format that search and code history
+tools can read. The export works offline and does not start a model call.
+
+```sh
+gemini sessions export --format agent-session --session SESSION_ID
+```
+
+This command writes one session to standard output. To save separate files, use
+`--output DIRECTORY`. Repeat `--session` to select several sessions. Without a
+selector, directory output includes all saved sessions in the current project.
+Existing files are refused. Files use private permissions and names derived from
+the session identity.
+
+Use `--input FILE` to read a specific transcript without loading global settings.
+Repeat it for several files. `--since` accepts an RFC 3339 timestamp and selects
+files by modification time. Missing sessions and ambiguous selections fail.
+
+The export keeps recorded messages, tool requests and available results. Updated
+results appear where their final version was saved. Retained work stays available
+after a rewind. Gaps identify corrupt or incomplete history.
+
+Saved conversations do not contain every approval, setting, model call or file
+edit. The export declares these limits. It supports current JSONL recordings and
+legacy JSON files. Select a single recording segment when several files share a
+session identity.
+
+Known credentials and opaque provider state are excluded. Review the export
+before sharing because a filter cannot recognize every secret in ordinary text.
